    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP tonight centers squarely on **Brice Turang**, who stands as our clear-cut elite play with a score of 65.44. Despite the high-leverage matchup against the stuff of Roki Sasaki, **Brice Turang** earns a massive boost due to his projected spot in the #2 hole and, more importantly, his elite stolen base potential. The algorithm projects a significant advantage against the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, making **Brice Turang** our primary engine for a category where we remain hyper-aggressive. Meanwhile, **Travis Bazzana** (56.66) also grades out strongly, benefiting from a favorable 4.43 xERA matchup against the opposition; the model is buying his recent momentum and a platoon edge that allows him to outperform his base projection by double-digit percentage points. \n\nWe are exercising caution with **Jose Caballero** (44.61) and **Josh Naylor** (54.98), both of whom face high-tier pitching in the form of Logan Gilbert and Max Fried, respectively. While **Josh Naylor** holds value in the #5 spot, his score is tempered by the southpaw\u2019s ability to stifle production. The most difficult decision rested on the marginal start of **Jose Caballero**; while his raw output against Gilbert is sub-optimal, he remains in the lineup due to the scarcity of speed, narrowly edging out depth options. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** and **Trevor Story**, who remain sidelined on the IL, while **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak** are unavailable today due to team off-days. With the **Brice Turang** lineup pending confirmation, we are prepared to pivot if his spot in the order shifts, but for now, we are counting on his ability to disrupt the basepaths against a premium arm to anchor our 5x5 effort.",
